The attached image (Figure 5) demonstrates that Nano-11 enhances the uptake of adsorbed antigens by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs). Plot (A) shows flow cytometry dot plots, where BMDCs incubated with Nano-11-adsorbed ovalbumin (OVA) exhibit a pronounced increase in cells containing both Nano-11 and OVA, compared to cells exposed to soluble OVA or Nano-11 alone. Plot (B), a histogram of FITC-OVA fluorescence, quantifies this, illustrating a significant shift to higher fluorescence for BMDCs incubated with Nano-11-adsorbed OVA, indicating enhanced intracellular delivery of the antigen. This supports Nano-11's role as an effective vaccine delivery vehicle.